 "q-40372" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067267/assets/9ba3d1f0eebdfc82c40f36bdbe16896ca15516b623c695b72c331861955329bc.png)\n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B},\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{C\\to B}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B.$\n\nSolving this equation for $[T]_{B},$ we obtain the alternative formulation\n\n$$\n[T]_{B}={P}_{C\\to B}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067267/state.json" "file_sha256" "436ec3446d638b7de18863d022545e96a0facaf2d1108f9fd91583e9b9917daa"} {"question" "q-40372" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067267/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "44993624314b48147f859c371ebc2b814f7547ce32669e025d29143f55cb199f"} {"question" "q-40372" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067267/state.json" "file_sha256" "436ec3446d638b7de18863d022545e96a0facaf2d1108f9fd91583e9b9917daa"} {"question" "q-40372" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067267/state.json" "file_sha256" "436ec3446d638b7de18863d022545e96a0facaf2d1108f9fd91583e9b9917daa"} {"question" "q-40372" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067267/state.json" "file_sha256" "436ec3446d638b7de18863d022545e96a0facaf2d1108f9fd91583e9b9917daa"} {"question" "q-38454" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n[T]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{P}_{C\\to B}=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $[T]_{C}$ of a linear transformation $T$ with respect to the basis $C$ and the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{C\\to B}$ shown above. Find the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $B.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067267/state.json" "file_sha256" "436ec3446d638b7de18863d022545e96a0facaf2d1108f9fd91583e9b9917daa"} {"question" "q-38454" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067267/assets/2e82c232614bec8a98f079ea56d7913ee13e7b457e33e418198278d2e369fc5c.png)\n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}.\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{C\\to B}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B.$\n\nOur goal is to compute $[T]_{B}.$ Solving this equation for $[T]_{B},$ we obtain the alternative formulation\n\n$$\n[T]_{B}={P}_{C\\to B}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{C\\to B}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{C\\to B}^{-1} & ={[\\begin{aligned}5 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot 5-1\\cdot 6}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -6 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 6 \\\\ 1 & -5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{B} & ={P}_{C\\to B}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 6 \\\\ 1 & -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -8 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 6 \\\\ 1 & -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 34 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067267/state.json" "file_sha256" "436ec3446d638b7de18863d022545e96a0facaf2d1108f9fd91583e9b9917daa"} {"question" "q-38454" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067267/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "44993624314b48147f859c371ebc2b814f7547ce32669e025d29143f55cb199f"} {"question" "q-38454" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067267/state.json" "file_sha256" "436ec3446d638b7de18863d022545e96a0facaf2d1108f9fd91583e9b9917daa"} {"question" "q-38454" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-7 & -26 \\\\ -1 & -5\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 16 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 34 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-9 & -16 \\\\ -1 & -4\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}23 & -26 \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067267/state.json" "file_sha256" "436ec3446d638b7de18863d022545e96a0facaf2d1108f9fd91583e9b9917daa"} {"question" "q-38454" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 34 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067267/state.json" "file_sha256" "436ec3446d638b7de18863d022545e96a0facaf2d1108f9fd91583e9b9917daa"} {"question" "q-97114" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n[T]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{P}_{C\\to B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $[T]_{C}$ of a linear transformation $T$ with respect to the basis $C$ and the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{C\\to B}$ shown above. Find the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $B.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067267/state.json" "file_sha256" "436ec3446d638b7de18863d022545e96a0facaf2d1108f9fd91583e9b9917daa"} {"question" "q-97114" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067267/assets/2e82c232614bec8a98f079ea56d7913ee13e7b457e33e418198278d2e369fc5c.png)\n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}.\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{C\\to B}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B.$\n\nOur goal is to compute $[T]_{B}.$ Solving this equation for $[T]_{B},$ we obtain the alternative formulation\n\n$$\n[T]_{B}={P}_{C\\to B}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{C\\to B}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{C\\to B}^{-1} & ={[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\cdot 3-2\\cdot 4}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{B} & ={P}_{C\\to B}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 8 \\\\ -8 & 11\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067267/state.json" "file_sha256" "436ec3446d638b7de18863d022545e96a0facaf2d1108f9fd91583e9b9917daa"} {"question" "q-97114" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067267/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "44993624314b48147f859c371ebc2b814f7547ce32669e025d29143f55cb199f"} {"question" "q-97114" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067267/state.json" "file_sha256" "436ec3446d638b7de18863d022545e96a0facaf2d1108f9fd91583e9b9917daa"} {"question" "q-97114" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -16 \\\\ 4 & 11\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -8 \\\\ -4 & -5\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 8 \\\\ -8 & 11\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}14 & -20 \\\\ -12 & 17\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067267/state.json" "file_sha256" "436ec3446d638b7de18863d022545e96a0facaf2d1108f9fd91583e9b9917daa"} {"question" "q-97114" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 8 \\\\ -8 & 11\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067267/state.json" "file_sha256" "436ec3446d638b7de18863d022545e96a0facaf2d1108f9fd91583e9b9917daa"} {"question" "q-38356" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n[T]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 6 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $[T]_{B}$ of a linear transformation $T$ with respect to the basis $B$ and the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{B\\to C}$ shown above. Find the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067267/state.json" "file_sha256" "436ec3446d638b7de18863d022545e96a0facaf2d1108f9fd91583e9b9917daa"} {"question" "q-38356" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067267/assets/1b81504d6fdcabee0e1f586fef3dd2af5a57a8411ba4d22429e00e09b171a4d1.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}\\,,\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{B\\to C}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$\n\nOur goal is to compute $[T]_{C}.$ First, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} & ={[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-1)\\cdot (-1)-2\\cdot 1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{C} & ={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-5 & 6 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067267/state.json" "file_sha256" "436ec3446d638b7de18863d022545e96a0facaf2d1108f9fd91583e9b9917daa"} {"question" "q-38356" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067267/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "44993624314b48147f859c371ebc2b814f7547ce32669e025d29143f55cb199f"} {"question" "q-38356" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/questio